From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] core: SIT port type on the cpif subsystem (local)

Adds MM_PORT_TYPE_SIT / MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_SIT and MM_PORT_SUBSYS_CPIF for
the SIT control channel of Samsung Shannon modems (Google Pixel cpif):
ports tagged ID_MM_PORT_TYPE_SIT are never probed and are supported by
plugins with MM_PLUGIN_ALLOWED_SIT, which also skip the driver filter
(cpif nodes and rmnet are driverless virtual devices); the SIT port is the
primary port when there is no AT/QMI/MBIM port. Local, not upstreamed.
---
diff --git a/include/ModemManager-enums.h b/include/ModemManager-enums.h
index e86b7752..cd366714 100644
--- a/include/ModemManager-enums.h
+++ b/include/ModemManager-enums.h
@@ -670,6 +670,7 @@ typedef enum { /*< underscore_name=mm_modem_band >*/
  * @MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_AUDIO: Audio port. Since 1.12.
  * @MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_IGNORED: Ignored port. Since 1.16.
  * @MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_XMMRPC: Control protocol for Intel XMM modems. Since 1.24.
+ * @MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_SIT: SIT control protocol for Samsung Shannon modems (local).
  *
  * Type of modem port.
  *
@@ -686,6 +687,7 @@ typedef enum { /*< underscore_name=mm_modem_port_type >*/
     MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_AUDIO   = 8,
     MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_IGNORED = 9,
     MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_XMMRPC  = 10,
+    MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_SIT     = 11,
 } MMModemPortType;
 
